Docsie Self-Hosted Application License — Free Tier
Effective September 8, 2026

The Docsie application, container images and embedded application components
remain proprietary. No open-source license to those components is granted.

Likalo LLC grants you a non-exclusive right to install and use Docsie Self-Hosted
on infrastructure you control, free of license fees for up to 10 named workspace
users and 25 individual named portal users per installation. Workspace users
create and manage content. Portal users authenticate to access training and
secure documentation; this allowance counts individual people, not tenant
organizations or concurrent sessions. Each person counts once in each applicable
allowance across the installation, even if they access multiple workspaces or
portals. A person using both roles counts toward both allowances.

Public knowledge-base views are unlimited. Anonymous public documentation
viewers do not consume either user allowance. Personal and commercial use are
permitted, including internal use by a team within a company. There is no time
limit on this free tier, and it is not a time-limited trial.

Exceeding either 10 named workspace users or 25 individual named portal users
requires a paid commercial license from Docsie. Infrastructure, storage and
model inference costs remain your responsibility.

This notice grants no right to resell Docsie or offer Docsie itself as a hosted
service to third parties. Keep proprietary notices intact. Rights not expressly
